      "message": "this breaks the connection on the advertiser side\n\nOn the advertiser side, a device wants to accept connection from unknown remote devices\n\nHence the incoming device address will not be in the filter allow list\n\nMaybe we should also check if there was\n* a prior extended create connection and a create connection cancel before the extended create connection was completed \n* AND if the device was in filter accept list when extended create connection was sent, but is no longer in filter accept list now\n* AND whether there is an ongoing connectable BLE advertisement?\n\nTo summarize, we should only disconnect a connection if\n\n* We are not sending connectable advertisement\n* AND the incoming connected device is no longer in local filter accept list",
